# Copy this file to .env and fill in the keys you have. All are optional —
# the app runs fine with none; those museums just stay disabled.
#
# These are SERVER-side vars (no VITE_ prefix, deliberately). They're read
# only by api/_shared/sources.ts and never reach the browser — the client
# calls /api/museum instead of the museum directly. Don't add a VITE_ prefix
# to any of them: that would compile the key straight into the public bundle.

# Smithsonian Institution Open Access
# Free, instant, self-serve signup at https://api.data.gov/signup/
# (registers you for the whole api.data.gov platform, Smithsonian included).
# The key is issued on the spot and emailed to you.
SMITHSONIAN_API_KEY=

# Harvard Art Museums
# Requested via a Google Form linked from https://github.com/harvardartmuseums/api-docs
# — this is manual/human-approved, not instant. Their terms restrict use to
# non-commercial purposes, cap you at 2500 requests/day, and forbid caching
# results beyond two weeks.
HARVARD_API_KEY=

# Europeana
# Free, but not auto-issued on signup: register a Europeana account at
# https://www.europeana.eu/en/for-developers and confirm the email, then
# request a key from the API key section of your account. A confirmation
# email arrives and the key appears there — fast, but it is a
# request-and-approve step, unlike Smithsonian's. A higher-rate "project key"
# can be requested from the same place.
# Aggregates ~4000 European institutions; per-item licensing varies
# (CC0/PDM/CC-BY/CC-BY-SA), unlike this app's CC0-only sources.
EUROPEANA_API_KEY=
